<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-04%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-04> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Sample feed: Material in compatible syringe; chemical compatibility depends on syringe and tubing; states: Loaded syringe; material composition not prescribed; phase: Fluid; phase/composition not comprehensively specified
DC power: 12 V DC; 800 mA at full load; states: Power connected or disconnected; country-specific external adapter
Syringe internal diameter: 0.100–50.00 mm; states: Numeric setting; syringe-specific
Flow-rate setting: 0.73 µL/h with 1 mL B-D syringe to 1699 mL/h with 60 mL B-D syringe (manual edition); states: Numeric rate; syringe-dependent limits
Dispense target and direction: VOL target; DIR INF/WDR/REV/STK; states: Infuse, withdraw, reverse or sticky direction; target volume is numeric
Program definition: Up to 41 phases; phase functions include rate, fill, increment/decrement, stop, jump, loop, pause, conditional/event and output functions; states: RAT/FIL/INC/DEC/STP/JMP/PRI/PRL/LPS/LOP/LPE/PAS/IF/EVN/EVS/EVR/CLD/TRG/BEP/OUT; details depend on firmware
Operational trigger, pin 2: TTL LOW 0–1.5 V; HIGH 3.5–5.25 V; stable level ≥100 ms; states: FT/FH/F2/LE/ST/T2/SP/P2/RL/RH/SL/SH/OF; event-trap modes ET/BT also documented; edge meaning is mode-dependent
Direction input, pin 3: TTL LOW 0–1.5 V; HIGH 3.5–5.25 V; states: dr:rE: falling edge infuse, rising edge withdraw; dr:dU reverses that mapping
Event and program inputs, pins 4 and 6: TTL LOW 0–1.5 V; HIGH 3.5–5.25 V; states: Pin 4 event/user input; pin 6 conditional or user input, also keypad lockout
RS-232 commands and responses: 300/1200/2400/9600/19200 baud; up to 100 pumps; states: Commands RUN/STP/PUR; DIS/VER/IN queries; status/error responses; basic or safe communications mode""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-04%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-04> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """RS-232 commands and responses: 300/1200/2400/9600/19200 baud; up to 100 pumps; states: Commands RUN/STP/PUR; DIS/VER/IN queries; status/error responses; basic or safe communications mode
Dispensed/withdrawn material: Flow follows the configured direction and syringe-dependent rate; states: Infusing, withdrawing or stopped; phase: Fluid; phase/composition depends on loaded sample
Program output, pin 5: User/program-defined logic output; states: LOW or HIGH; OUT 5 {0|1}
Motor-running output, pin 7: RUN.0 or RUN.1 mapping; states: RUN.0 HIGH=pumping, LOW=not pumping; RUN.1 HIGH=pumping or pause timer, LOW=program stopped/paused
Direction output, pin 8: Logic direction indication; states: HIGH=infuse; LOW=withdraw
Dispensed-volume/status response: DIS reports dispensed volume; firmware/status responses available through RS-232; states: Separate infuse/withdraw counters; status responses depend on command and pump state
Buzzer: BUZ controls audible notification; states: Off, continuous, or specified number of beeps""" .

