<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-07%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-07> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Liquid in one or two syringes, selected syringe type/diameter, infusion rate and target volume or time. Legato 200 is INFUSE ONLY; do not assign Legato 210 withdrawal or 210P/270P programming features. Supply: 100–240 VAC, 50–60 Hz. USB/RS-232 and a 15-pin I/O/TTL connector are documented for the family; the external footswitch can toggle run/stop or follow rising/falling edges. The 0–10 V speed-control input is a factory option.
Source: Manuals/KDS Legato 200 Series_5617-002REV2.0.pdf, PDF pp. 6, 8, 11, 17–19, 62–65, 79, 89.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-07%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-07> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Infused liquid; pump/run indication, programmed trigger outputs where supported, completion and stall/power-failure messages. Family TTL outputs are Boolean high/low; only functions enabled by the installed Legato 200 configuration apply. No withdrawal stream is produced by this infuse-only model.
Source: Manuals/KDS Legato 200 Series_5617-002REV2.0.pdf, PDF pp. 6, 8, 11, 17–19, 62–65, 79, 89.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-07%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-07> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """pL/min, µL/min, mL/min and mL/h (flow selections/range); µL and mL (syringe/target volume); mm (syringe diameter); s/min/h (time); V, Hz and W (supply/optional control); TTL high/low (dimensionless). Flow limits depend on syringe size.
Source: Manuals/KDS Legato 200 Series_5617-002REV2.0.pdf, PDF pp. 6, 8, 11, 17–19, 62–65, 79, 89.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-08%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-08> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Liquid in one or two syringes; syringe type, inside diameter and volume; infusion/withdrawal rate; target volume. Legato 210 (788210) supports infuse only, withdraw only, infuse/withdraw, withdraw/infuse and continuous modes, and stores one program. Target time is available in infusion-only or withdrawal-only mode. Supply: 100–240 VAC, 50–60 Hz. USB/RS-232 ASCII commands control run/stop and infusion/withdrawal settings. Family 15-pin I/O: direction input rising edge = infuse, falling edge = refill; footswitch can toggle run/stop or start/stop on configured edges; trigger input is TTL high/low. Listed input thresholds: HIGH ≥2 V, LOW ≤0.4 V. Multi-program/advanced 210P features and the 0–10 V analog-input option listed only for 788212/788272 are not assigned to the standard 210. Installed controller/firmware applicability must be checked.
Source: Manuals/KDS Legato 200 Series_5617-002REV2.0.pdf, PDF pp. 6, 8, 11, 17–19, 62–65, 79, 89. Model scope: Legato 210 (788210).""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-08%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-08> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Infused or withdrawn liquid, according to the selected Legato 210 mode; infused/withdrawn volume, elapsed time and current-rate responses. Serial STATUS reports rate, time, volume, infusion/withdrawal direction with idle/running state, limit switch, stall, trigger state and target reached. Family TTL outputs: direction HIGH = refill, LOW = infuse; sync rising edge = start infuse, falling edge = start refill; run output active LOW = running. Trigger outputs 1/2 can be set HIGH/LOW by serial command and default LOW. Listed output levels: HIGH ≥3.8 V, LOW ≤0.4 V, source/sink current ≤6 mA. Event-program behavior remains configuration-specific. Simultaneous push/pull capability of the 270 and advanced multi-program features of the 210P are not assumed.
Source: Manuals/KDS Legato 200 Series_5617-002REV2.0.pdf, PDF pp. 6, 8, 11, 17–19, 62–65, 79, 89. Model scope: Legato 210 (788210).""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-08%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-08> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """Flow-rate command units: pL, nL, µL or mL per second, minute or hour (syringe-dependent limits). Syringe/target and infused/withdrawn volume: µL or mL; syringe diameter: mm. Time: s and h:m:s. Raw serial STATUS: fL/s (rate), ms (time), fL (volume), plus dimensionless state flags. Electrical supply/I/O ratings: V/VAC, Hz, W, µA and mA; TTL HIGH/LOW and direction/run/target flags are dimensionless. Scope: Legato 210 using the documented 200-series interface, not the 210P/270P analog option.
Source: Manuals/KDS Legato 200 Series_5617-002REV2.0.pdf, PDF pp. 6, 8, 11, 17–19, 62–65, 79, 89. Model scope: Legato 210 (788210).""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-09%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
