<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M20-03%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M20-03> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Sample and a suitable process tube; vacuum or flowing gas through the installed flanges. Temperature program contains up to 30 temperature/time segments. Power-lock and furnace relay turn on/off; controller commands enter RUN, HOLD/resume or STOP. The series manual calls for a configured 208–240 V single-phase line in 110 V regions. Gas-pressure limits and atmosphere restrictions must follow the exact tube/flange configuration.
Source: Manuals/MTI OTF-1200X__linked-manual__94143f6f5d.pdf, PDF pp. 4, 8, 11–17, 20–21.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M20-03%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M20-03> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Thermally treated sample; PV display shows current chamber temperature and SV shows the programmed value/state. RUN advances segments; HOLD pauses/resumes; STOP halts the program; relay-off removes heater power. Complete remote-I/O pins are not enumerated in this series manual.
Source: Manuals/MTI OTF-1200X__linked-manual__94143f6f5d.pdf, PDF pp. 4, 8, 11–17, 20–21.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M20-03%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M20-03> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """°C (process temperature); min and s (profile/timing parameters); °C/min (heating/cooling rate); V and Hz (supply); atm or MPa (tube-pressure restrictions). The pressure restrictions are engineering limits, not proof of a calibrated pressure-output channel.
Source: Manuals/MTI OTF-1200X__linked-manual__94143f6f5d.pdf, PDF pp. 4, 8, 11–17, 20–21.""" .

