<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M23-09%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M23-09> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Substrate and sputter targets; process-gas supply, vacuum-pump connections and RF/DC sputtering power. The brochure lists two 2-inch magnetron cathodes with independent shutters, 500 W RF and 1 kW DC supplies, and substrate rotation adjustable from 0 to 25 rpm. A microprocessor PLC controls vacuum valves and auto-pump/auto-vent sequencing with software interlocks. The optional DVO/CS automation package is not assumed installed.
Source: Manuals/Discovery-18.pdf, PDF pp. 1 and 4, visually reviewed.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M23-09%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M23-09> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Sputtered coating on the substrate; digital mass-flow and vacuum-pressure readouts. Valve/pump/vent and shutter operation are described, but the brochure does not enumerate the electrical ready/alarm/pin-state map.
Source: Manuals/Discovery-18.pdf, PDF pp. 1 and 4, visually reviewed.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M23-09%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M23-09> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """Torr (vacuum pressure); L/s and cfm (pumping speed); rpm (substrate rotation); W/kW (RF/DC power); V and A (DC supply rating); in (target/substrate geometry).
Source: Manuals/Discovery-18.pdf, PDF pp. 1 and 4, visually reviewed.""" .

