<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M34-09%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M34-09> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Nanoparticle suspension/solution in the appropriate cell. Particle sizing requires 0.9 mL in the standard cell or 20 µL in the micro-volume cell; zeta analysis requires 0.7 mL in a standard glass cell or 130 µL in a disposable cell. Peltier temperature control is specified from 0 to 90 °C. The ELSZ-PT pH/additive autotitrator and surface-zeta accessory are optional, not assumed installed. The brochure does not provide the command, trigger or ready/alarm state map.
Source: Manuals/Otsuka-ELSZ2000-brochure-Hi-Res.pdf, PDF pp. 9–11, visually reviewed.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M34-09%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M34-09> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """DLS particle size/size distribution, electrophoretic zeta potential and molecular-weight analysis by the described DLS/SLS methods. Particle-size measurement and zeta analysis use distinct optical configurations; samples, concentration and calibration affect reported results. No electrical output-state/pin map is supplied.
Source: Manuals/Otsuka-ELSZ2000-brochure-Hi-Res.pdf, PDF pp. 9–11, visually reviewed.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M34-09%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M34-09> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """nm (particle size and laser wavelength); mV (zeta potential); Da/MDa (molecular weight); mL/µL (sample volume); °C (sample temperature); degrees (scattering angle); % (concentration); mW (specified laser power). Optional autotitrator pH is not treated as an installed base-instrument output.
Source: Manuals/Otsuka-ELSZ2000-brochure-Hi-Res.pdf, PDF pp. 9–11, visually reviewed.""" .

