<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-014%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-014> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Conductive workpiece; 0.18 mm (0.007 in) reusable molybdenum wire; deionized water with the specified additive for the 434W (do not transfer the pure-water 434WW specification). On-board CAD/CNC instructions, USB/LAN DXF and MDI inputs. Flyer lists 220 V, three-phase, 60 Hz, 3–5 kVA input for the four-axis family, with no chiller or air-pressure requirement. 434W travel: X 400, Y 320, Z 410 mm; maximum workpiece mass 600 kg.
Source: Manuals/EDMMax Fast Wire Flyer (new).pdf; I, PDF pp. 1–2, visually reviewed, and the exact 434W seller listing.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-014%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-014> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Four-axis discharge-cut workpiece, including LPBF parts separated from build plates; wire recirculates, and swarf is carried into the dielectric filtration system. Cut taper is approximately ±3°. The flyer does not define machine-ready, alarm or numerical-control pin states.
Source: Manuals/EDMMax Fast Wire Flyer (new).pdf; I, PDF pp. 1–2, visually reviewed, and the exact 434W seller listing.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-014%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-014> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """mm and in (wire diameter and axis travel); kg and lb (workpiece mass); degrees (taper); m/s (wire speed, family description); V, Hz and kVA (supply). No cutting-current or voltage measurement range is supplied.
Source: Manuals/EDMMax Fast Wire Flyer (new).pdf; I, PDF pp. 1–2, visually reviewed, and the exact 434W seller listing.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-015%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-015> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Tool/workpiece load and motion commands through the specified FANUC RJ2/RJ3 controller. The LR Mate 200i is a six-axis arm; cart interfaces and the full electrical I/O map are not described by this arm-only seller specification.
Source: I, LR Mate 200i Details, Motion Speed and Motion Range.""" .

