<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-026%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-026> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Payloads/end effectors for two FR3 arms and the mobile base; teleoperation or learned-policy commands through the integrated software. The manufacturer sheet lists 3 kg payload per arm, 100 kg base payload, maximum base speed 1.75 m/s and 1 kHz FCI. Wi-Fi, Ethernet, USB and Bluetooth are listed. Installed controller commands, safety-state guards and utility/power ratings are not enumerated in this two-page sheet.
Source: I, Mobile FR3 Duo manufacturer sheet, PDF pp. 1–2.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-026%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-026> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Coordinated dual-arm motion and omnidirectional base motion; sensing includes 14 arm-torque sensors, two lidars, seven cameras and one IMU. The exact raw signal fields, sensor units/scaling and ready/error states require the installed FCI/sensor documentation.
Source: I, Mobile FR3 Duo manufacturer sheet, PDF pp. 1–2.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-026%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-026> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """kg (arm/base payload); m/s (base travel speed); kHz (FCI frequency). Detailed torque, pose, image and IMU output units are not stated in the linked product sheet.
Source: I, Mobile FR3 Duo manufacturer sheet, PDF pp. 1–2.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-027%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-027> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """The linked source is the MultiPort cell kit: electrolyte, a metal working-electrode specimen, graphite counter electrode and a separately selected reference electrode. Optional purge/blanket gas requires a vent; the cell is not a pressure vessel. Optional jacket accepts circulating bath fluid; spare ports accept a thermometer/pH probe or reactant addition. Electrode leads connect to a separate potentiostat. Gas modes are purge, blanket and vent; no electronic command-state map is provided for the passive cell.
Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-027%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-027> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Electrode potential/current response is conveyed to the connected potentiostat; corrosion/impedance results depend on that instrument and method. The passive cell itself does not acquire or export digital measurements. Purge gas exits the vent; the reacted electrolyte/specimen remain in the cell. The unspecified inventory row does not confirm the MultiPort model or an eight-channel potentiostat.
Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-027%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-027> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """mL (MultiPort standard operating volume: 1000 mL); cm² or in² (nominal gasket-covered electrode area); mm/in (specimen geometry). Voltage, current, impedance, temperature and pH units/ranges depend on separately installed measuring instruments.
Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.""" .

