<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-040%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-040> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """PARTIAL FAMILY REFERENCE — installed CB1-04 controller not verified. The manual’s safety-shutter declaration expressly includes CARBIDE CB1 among the listed families. For the documented shutter subsystem, control is by shutter switch or software; interruption of the remote-interlock circuit is abnormal and requires a manual reset or software reset to restore shutter operation. Use this as family-level safety evidence only: the exact CB1-04 power, cooling, trigger and control-pin inputs remain unestablished.
Source: Manuals2/CARBIDE-CB3-80W-User-Manual (1).pdf, PDF pp. 84–89 and 107.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-040%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-040> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """PARTIAL FAMILY REFERENCE — installed CB1-04 controller not verified. The listed safety function is emergency-stop activation on shutter failure. In the documented safety-shutter subsystem, a detected failure interrupts SHUTTER ERROR OUTPUTS; an external power-switching/emergency-stop circuit is needed to remove laser power, and shutter function is restored by a complete controller power cycle. Exact CB1-04 laser-output specifications, connector levels and status-pin mappings are not established; CB3-80W performance limits were not transferred.
Source: Manuals2/CARBIDE-CB3-80W-User-Manual (1).pdf, PDF pp. 84–89 and 107.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-040%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-040> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value "CPA-based Yb:KGW Femtosecond / Picosecond Laser; 1028 nm – 1030 nm; Tunable from 290 fs to 10 ps; Pulse energy > 100 µJ; Repetition rate 100 kHz to 1000 kHz; Power requirements 110 to 220 VAC, 50/60 Hz (up to 300 W max draw);" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-041%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-041> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """DC electrical power, specified cooling and external CTRL PWM command. Command LOW 0–0.5 VDC=beam off; HIGH 3.5–10 VDC=beam on, subject to interlocks/faults. Standard PWM 5 kHz, maximum 20 kHz; duty cycle controls power. Analog 0–10 V / 4–20 mA control requires a UC-2000 intermediary.
Source: H, PDF pp. 16, 38–39, 44–49.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-041%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-041> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """CO₂ laser beam (enabled/disabled by gating, shutter/interlocks and fault shutdown). Temperature warning at DB-9 pin 5 goes LOW at 54±2 °C and remains low until temperature drops below the specified reset threshold. Other outputs depend on connector/model configuration.
Source: H, PDF pp. 16, 38–39, 44–49.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-041%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-041> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """V DC; kHz/Hz (PWM repetition); % (duty cycle); µs (pulse timing); °C/°F (thermal conditions); µm (optical wavelength); mA (UC-2000-mediated analog control)
Source: H, PDF pp. 16, 38–39, 44–49.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-042%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-042> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """End effector and workpiece: Tool/workpiece load within the model payload and center-of-gravity envelope; states: Configured payload and center of gravity; workpiece state depends on attached tool; phase: Not prescribed by robot manual
Control-box digital/safety/configurable inputs: PNP; input voltage −3–30 V; states: OFF region −3–5 V; ON region 11–30 V; 5–11 V is not a valid guaranteed logic region
Control-box analog inputs: Voltage mode 0–10 V or current mode 4–20 mA; 12-bit resolution; states: Voltage/current mode selected in GUI
Tool digital inputs: PNP with weak pull-down; floating input reads LOW; states: LOW ≤2.0 V; HIGH ≥5.5 V within permitted input range −0.5–26 V
Robot motion/program configuration: Joint/TCP moves, payload and tool/installation settings in PolyScope; states: Program/installation dependent; this extract does not enumerate all PolyScope commands or safety functions
Additional documented controls/states: manual/automatic operating mode, remote/local control.
Source: Manuals/Universal Robots UR12e__linked-manual__76e09f695d.pdf, PDF p. 21, 25.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-042%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-042> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Control-box analog outputs: Voltage mode 0–10 V or current mode 4–20 mA; 12-bit resolution; states: Voltage/current output mode selected; range and load constraints apply
Control-box digital outputs: PNP; current 0–1 A with specified loads; states: HIGH/LOW; voltage drop and leakage limits given in manual
Tool digital outputs: Sinking NPN, sourcing PNP or push/pull; states: NPN active=LOW/inactive=open; PNP active=HIGH/inactive=open; push/pull active=HIGH/inactive=LOW; emergency stop=high impedance
Tool power supply: Selectable 0/12/24 V; specified single-/dual-pin current limits; states: Off, 12 V or 24 V; dual-pin mode changes output-pin availability
Tool/workpiece motion: Six-joint robot motion within configured workspace; states: Trajectory and stop conditions are program/safety-configuration dependent; phase: Workpiece phase is not prescribed""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-042%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-042> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value "A; V; bit; joint count; kg; m/s; mA; mm; °; °/s; Ω" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-043%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-043> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Workload: payload mounted on the mobile base (rated 100 kg). Power: 24 V battery. Commands: forward/reverse linear velocity and left/right angular velocity through CAN 2.0B at 500 kbit/s or the RC handset; emergency stop must be released. Feedback modes are standby=0x00, CAN=0x01 and RC=0x02. RC takes priority over CAN. Motion-command timeout after 500 ms sets velocity to zero.
Source: H, PDF pp. 3, 7–8, 11–19, 22–26, 34.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-043%3Aoutputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-043> ;
    schema:name "Output and output states" ;
    schema:propertyID "outputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Chassis translation/rotation; CAN feedback for actual linear/angular velocity, battery voltage, chassis/control-mode status, fault bits and motor information. Fault bits use 0=normal/no alarm and 1=fault/alarm. Feedback motor speed is in rpm; the side interface also provides 24 V expansion power.
Source: H, PDF pp. 3, 7–8, 11–19, 22–26, 34.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-043%3Aunits_of_measure> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-043> ;
    schema:name "Measuring units" ;
    schema:propertyID "units_of_measure" ;
    schema:value """mm/s (CAN linear velocity); 0.001 rad/s (CAN angular-velocity scaling); m/s (rated travel speed); rpm (motor feedback); V (battery, reported with ×10 integer scaling); A (motor current); °C (temperature); kg (payload); ms (command timing); kbit/s (CAN bitrate); coded/Boolean status flags (dimensionless)
Source: H, PDF pp. 3, 7–8, 11–19, 22–26, 34.""" .

<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-044%3Ainputs_and_states> a schema:PropertyValue ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-044> ;
    schema:name "Input and input states" ;
    schema:propertyID "inputs_and_states" ;
    schema:value """Specimens/plates and a mounted end effector for a six-joint robotic manipulator; programmed pick-up, transport and placement. The inventory gives the intended work, but both linked FANUC documents were unavailable in this sweep, so supply, safety-input and motion-command states are not established.
Source: Instrument Inventory Table (final).docx, Automation / FANUC CRX-10iA entry.""" .

