<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M34-09> a icon:InputOutputProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Otsuka ELSZ-2000 — input/output metadata" ;
    dct:identifier "M34-09" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv> ;
    icon:importedDate "2026-10-30" ;
    icon:inputDescription """Nanoparticle suspension/solution in the appropriate cell. Particle sizing requires 0.9 mL in the standard cell or 20 µL in the micro-volume cell; zeta analysis requires 0.7 mL in a standard glass cell or 130 µL in a disposable cell. Peltier temperature control is specified from 0 to 90 °C. The ELSZ-PT pH/additive autotitrator and surface-zeta accessory are optional, not assumed installed. The brochure does not provide the command, trigger or ready/alarm state map.
Source: Manuals/Otsuka-ELSZ2000-brochure-Hi-Res.pdf, PDF pp. 9–11, visually reviewed.""" ;
    icon:measuringUnitsDescription """nm (particle size and laser wavelength); mV (zeta potential); Da/MDa (molecular weight); mL/µL (sample volume); °C (sample temperature); degrees (scattering angle); % (concentration); mW (specified laser power). Optional autotitrator pH is not treated as an installed base-instrument output.
Source: Manuals/Otsuka-ELSZ2000-brochure-Hi-Res.pdf, PDF pp. 9–11, visually reviewed.""" ;
    icon:outputDescription """DLS particle size/size distribution, electrophoretic zeta potential and molecular-weight analysis by the described DLS/SLS methods. Particle-size measurement and zeta analysis use distinct optical configurations; samples, concentration and calibration affect reported results. No electrical output-state/pin map is supplied.
Source: Manuals/Otsuka-ELSZ2000-brochure-Hi-Res.pdf, PDF pp. 9–11, visually reviewed.""" ;
    icon:sourceModel "Otsuka ELSZ-2000" ;
    icon:sourceRow "749" ;
    icon:sourceSha256 "c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab" ;
    icon:sourceSheet "Sheet1" .

