    icon:importedDate "2026-10-30" ;
    icon:inputDescription """Conductive workpiece; 0.18 mm (0.007 in) reusable molybdenum wire; deionized water with the specified additive for the 434W (do not transfer the pure-water 434WW specification). On-board CAD/CNC instructions, USB/LAN DXF and MDI inputs. Flyer lists 220 V, three-phase, 60 Hz, 3–5 kVA input for the four-axis family, with no chiller or air-pressure requirement. 434W travel: X 400, Y 320, Z 410 mm; maximum workpiece mass 600 kg.
Source: Manuals/EDMMax Fast Wire Flyer (new).pdf; I, PDF pp. 1–2, visually reviewed, and the exact 434W seller listing.""" ;
    icon:measuringUnitsDescription """mm and in (wire diameter and axis travel); kg and lb (workpiece mass); degrees (taper); m/s (wire speed, family description); V, Hz and kVA (supply). No cutting-current or voltage measurement range is supplied.
Source: Manuals/EDMMax Fast Wire Flyer (new).pdf; I, PDF pp. 1–2, visually reviewed, and the exact 434W seller listing.""" ;
    icon:outputDescription """Four-axis discharge-cut workpiece, including LPBF parts separated from build plates; wire recirculates, and swarf is carried into the dielectric filtration system. Cut taper is approximately ±3°. The flyer does not define machine-ready, alarm or numerical-control pin states.
Source: Manuals/EDMMax Fast Wire Flyer (new).pdf; I, PDF pp. 1–2, visually reviewed, and the exact 434W seller listing.""" ;
    icon:sourceModel "EDMMax 434W Fast Wire EDM" ;
    icon:sourceRow "7" ;
