<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-024> a icon:InputOutputProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Standard Bots Core — input/output metadata" ;
    dct:identifier "REQ-EQ-024" ;
    dct:references <https://corehelp.standardbots.com/1-introduction.html> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv> ;
    icon:importedDate "2026-10-30" ;
    icon:inputDescription """Workload: end effector/workpiece within the 18 kg payload rating; six-axis motion program. Supported operating modes: collaborative or high-speed non-collaborative. Control box: 16 digital inputs and 4 analogue inputs, stated as 24 V tolerant; TCP/IP, Modbus TCP and EtherNet/IP are listed. Tool M8 8-pin connector: 2 digital inputs and 2 analogue inputs (24 V tolerant); RS-485/UART up to 10 Mbit/s. Controller supply: 90–264 VAC, 47–63 Hz; program/payload-dependent power 25–1500 W. Tool-I/O hardware is listed, but the April 2026 footnote says software support was forthcoming; confirm installed firmware. Input HIGH/LOW thresholds and analogue ranges/scaling are not specified.
Source: Manuals2/6ad0baa701069695bb0452a4_New Core Specs 202604.pdf, PDF p. 2.""" ;
    icon:measuringUnitsDescription """kg (payload); m/mm (reach, repeatability and geometry); degrees and °/s (joint range/speed); W/kW (power); V/VAC and A (electrical supply/I/O ratings); Hz (mains frequency); °C (temperature); %RH (humidity); Mbit/s (serial data rate). Channel counts/DOF are dimensionless. These are published operating/specification units; analogue scaling and digital logic thresholds are not given.
Source: Manuals2/6ad0baa701069695bb0452a4_New Core Specs 202604.pdf, PDF p. 2.""" ;
    icon:outputDescription """Commanded robot/tool motion, rated reach 1.3 m, maximum joint speed 435°/s, repeatability ±0.025 mm. Control box: 16 digital outputs, 24 V / 0.7 A continuous; combined supply limit 3 A with internal power or 12 A with external power. Tool: 2 digital outputs, open-drain or push-pull (listed 1 A rating); zero analogue outputs; tool power 12/24 V, 3 A continuous maximum. The tool hardware/software-support caveat also applies to these outputs. Default states, per-pin assignments, fault/ready meanings and calibrated position/force telemetry fields are not supplied by the sheet.
Source: Manuals2/6ad0baa701069695bb0452a4_New Core Specs 202604.pdf, PDF p. 2.""" ;
    icon:sourceModel "Standard Bots Core" ;
    icon:sourceRow "26" ;
    icon:sourceSha256 "c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab" ;
    icon:sourceSheet "Sheet1" .

