<https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/SW17-M35-0B6C77913DB3> a icon:InputOutputProfile ;
    rdfs:label "Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified) — input/output metadata" ;
    dct:identifier "SW17-M35-0B6C77913DB3" ;
    dct:references <https://www.oceanoptics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Flame-User-Manual.pdf> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv> ;
    icon:importedDate "2026-10-30" ;
    icon:inputDescription """Optical input through the SMA fibre connector; acquisition integration time, averaging and trigger selection from the host PC over USB or serial connection. USB provides power. Normal/free-run, external synchronous, external hardware-level and external hardware-edge triggering are documented. DD4 pin 2 accepts the external TTL trigger (5 or 3.3 V as specified); GPIO pins are not 5 V tolerant. Exact Flame-S/Flame-T detector, slit and wavelength configuration is unspecified in this row.
Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.""" ;
    icon:measuringUnitsDescription """nm (wavelength/resolution); µm (slit width); µs, ms and s (integration/trigger timing); Hz (scan rate); V and mA (electrical interface/power); detector counts and configured logic states (dimensionless). Detector-specific integration ranges must not be merged between Flame-S and Flame-T.
Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.""" ;
    icon:outputDescription """Wavelength-resolved spectra and derived absorbance/reflectance/emission through the host software, subject to calibration. Red LED steady=powered; green LED steady=ready and flashing=acquiring. Single/continuous strobe, lamp-enable, configurable GPIO and serial transmit are documented at the DD4 interface. Pin voltages/directions vary; refer to the pin table rather than treating every signal as 5 V TTL.
Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.""" ;
    icon:sourceModel "Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)" ;
    icon:sourceRow "738" ;
    icon:sourceSha256 "c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab" ;
    icon:sourceSheet "Sheet1" .

